eryone else when I was a  teenager it's the first year he started  playing basketball at summer camp  he didn't score one point in this whole  like summer and this tournament that he  played in and then he started doing  double the hours in the next year he was  like the highest scorer he was like it  was simple math I wasn't more talented I  simply put in more hours it's a good  transition to something else that he  said that I think is interesting where  he talked you were asking him about when  he was sort of hitting his stride and he  talks about this moment where Shaq is  injured for like eight games and he sort  I think forty over forty and eight  straight games or something like that  and then Phil Jackson calls him into the  office when Shaq comes back and  basically is like now you got to tone it  down because now Shaq is back and the  East plays different so when we get to  the finals we have to do this  differently and he you know you'd think  that he would just be like no we're  winning like crazy  I'm dominator than Shaq we don't even  need Shaq you know they had their own  problems later but but he basically was  like yeah so I listened to the to the  mentor that's what I wanted to get to  because you talked a lot about  mentorship he listened to the mentor in  this case Phil Jackson who had already  done this with Jordan and he dialed it  back and then of course they end up  exactly if you'd like to be inspired  motivated and educated by some of the  most successful people around the world  check out the school of greatness full  episode playlist right over here and if  you'd like to see Louis houses interview  with me click right over here and to get  notified of all future videos be sure to  subscribe and click the notification  bell
 

